Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbtp: gate main + INA230 12V rails on host power state

Patch 0020 gated the CPU/PCH VR rails, but the main board rails (MB_P3V3,
MB_P5V, MB_P12V via ADC) and the connector/hot-swap 12V monitors
(MB_C2/C3/C4_P12V_INA230, MB_CONN_P12V_INA230) are also fed from the host
power domain.  When the host powers off they collapse to ~0 and trip the
"Lower Critical going low" threshold, logging one SEL entry per rail on every
power-down (and again on power-up).  These are not real faults - the rails are
simply off with the host.

Add "PowerState": "On" so adcsensor/psusensor only sample and threshold-check
them while the host is powered.  Standby rails (*_STBY, MB_P3V_BAT) and the
hot-swap controller input (MB_HSC) are intentionally left ungated because they
are present whenever the PSU/PDB is powered.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform configuration]
